  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Temperature and volume curves are drawn for&nbsp;two thermodynamic processes. For the first process, it is a straight line and for the second, it is a rectangular hyperbola. The ratio of work done in the first process to the work done in the second process is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0010_54852a17be6d.jpg\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 141px;\" /></p>\r"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "2:1",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "3:1",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "4:1",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "3:2",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0010_1fd3ad6b5fe9.jpg\" style=\"width: 140px; height: 120px;\" /><br />The first process is a constant pressure process, hence<br />w<sub>1</sub> = nR(2T<sub>0</sub> - T<sub>0</sub>) = nRT<sub>0</sub><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0010_5d44c293d409.jpg\" style=\"width: 140px; height: 129px;\" /><br />The equation for the second process is<br /><math><mrow><mtext>T</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>c</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>V</mtext> </mrow></mfrac></mrow></math><br />Hence,&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mtext>P</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>nRT</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>V</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>nRc</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>V</mtext> <mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>∴&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo> <mtext>w</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <munderover> <mo>∫</mo> <msub> <mtext>V</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </msub> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <msub> <mtext>V</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </msub> </mrow> </munderover> <mtext>PdV</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>nRT</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>∴&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>w</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>w</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>2&nbsp;</mn> <mtext>:&nbsp;</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </math><br />∴&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;2 : 1"
  }
}